# youtube.targets  -- file-authoritative target list (Option A)
# YouTube channel IDs (UC...). Use the channel ID, not the @handle.
# Format:  channel_id | Display Name | priority    (name+priority optional)
# Blank lines and # comments ignored. Prefix a line with ! to disable it.
# Edit this file then `docker restart unifiedcollector_collector` to apply.
#
# NOTE: these 5 were DEMO/TEST channels (big public YouTubers), not your own.
# Replace them with channels you actually want to collect. The line marked !
# is a DEAD/DELETED channel (a typo of PewDiePie's ID) -- left disabled as a
# reminder; delete it whenever.

UC-lHJZR3Gqxm24_Vd_AJ5Yw | PewDiePie | 5
UCsXVk37bltHxD1rDPwtNM8Q | Kurzgesagt - In a Nutshell | 5
UCBJycsmduvYEL83R_U4JriQ | Marques Brownlee (MKBHD) | 5
UCsBjURrPoezykLs9EqgamOA | Fireship | 5

# DEAD channel (does not exist - YouTube API returns 0 items). Kept disabled:
!UC-lHJ7Fjz2afzjHnshG7W-w | DEAD/typo of PewDiePie | 1
